venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
db.sqlite3
# Manual DB snapshots (db_backup_before_*.sqlite3) carry real student data —
# never commit them. `db.sqlite3` above is kept for clarity.
*.sqlite3
.env
*.log
media/
staticfiles/
staticfiles/*
# Railway data dumps — real user data, never commit
railway_backup_*.json.gz

# Final droplet archive — real data and secrets, never commit
droplet_final_backup/

# ── Never commit, never deploy ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below carries either real user data or credentials. The repo is
# what Railway deploys from, so anything tracked here reaches the server and
# GitHub. Patterns are deliberately broad -- a backup named something nobody
# anticipated is exactly the one that leaks.
*.env
!.env.example
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.dump
*_backup*
*backup_*
backups/
*.pem
*.key
